# The pictures of getting-started.md: a plate sketched from the origin,
# held by two dimensions, extruded, a hole sketched on its top face and
# cut through, the top edges rounded, and the hole measured.
# Coordinates are those of the 600x600 headless window.
# The property browser is widened so that its longest rows show whole.
size tw 720 600
shot getting-started-1-window
# The video of steps 2 to 5 (scripts/regen-guide-videos.sh).
video start getting-started-plate
caption Press R for a rectangle; click the origin, then the opposite corner.
# A rectangle from the origin; the first click lands on the origin
# point, which makes the corner coincident with it.
cursor on
key r
move 300 300
down L 300 300
up L 300 300
move 500 170
down L 500 170
up L 500 170
key esc
cursor off
shot getting-started-2-rectangle
caption Click the top side, press D, type 40 and press Enter.
# The top side's length.
cursor on
move 400 170
down L 400 170
up L 400 170
key d
edit 40
key esc
cursor off
shot getting-started-3-width gw
caption The same for the right-hand side: 25. The sketch is fully held.
# The right side's length: nothing is free any more.
move 500 235
down L 500 235
up L 500 235
key d
edit 25
key esc
shot getting-started-4-held
caption Shift+X extrudes it; click its depth's [change] and type 10.
# Extruded; its depth held at 10 from the group's screen.
key x shift
twmove 501 134
twdown L 501 134
twup L 501 134
twmove 501 134
twdown L 501 134
twup L 501 134
edit 10
view rotated
move 300 300
menu View|Zoom To Fit
leave
mark 614 122 714 22
shot getting-started-5-extruded
caption A plate 40 x 25 x 10.
pause 1
video end
# The top face picked, and a sketch started on it.
cursor on
click-face top face of g003-extrude
shot getting-started-6-face gw
menu Features|Sketch On Face
move 300 300
menu View|Zoom To Fit
menu View|Zoom Out
leave
cursor off
shot getting-started-7-on-face
# A circle, its diameter, and its centre's distances from two edges.
key c
move 340 290
down L 340 290
up L 340 290
move 396 290
down L 396 290
up L 396 290
key esc
move 396 290
down L 396 290
up L 396 290
key d
edit 10
key esc
move 340 290
down L 340 290
up L 340 290
move 420 75
down L 420 75
up L 420 75
key d
edit 20
key esc
move 340 299
down L 340 299
up L 340 299
move 208 450
down L 208 450
up L 208 450
key d
edit 12.5
key esc
leave
freedom
shot getting-started-8-hole-sketch
# Extruded as a difference, which turns the depth into the plate: 10
# deep, the circle's width; held there.
key x shift
twmove 78 234
twdown L 78 234
twup L 78 234
twmove 505 134
twdown L 505 134
twup L 505 134
twmove 510 134
twdown L 510 134
twup L 510 134
edit -10
view rotated
move 300 300
menu View|Zoom To Fit
leave
mark 614 122 714 22
mark 614 222 714 22
shot getting-started-9-cut
# The four top edges picked and rounded at 3 mm.
cursor on
move 297 190
down L 297 190
up L 297 190
move 513 224
down L 513 224
up L 513 224
move 418 341
down L 418 341
up L 418 341
move 202 307
down L 202 307
up L 202 307
dump
shot getting-started-10-edges gw
key f shift
twmove 168 134
twdown L 168 134
twup L 168 134
edit 3
leave
cursor off
shot getting-started-11-fillet
# Checked, then the hole's rim measured.
answer ok
menu Analyze|Check Solid
answer ok
menu Analyze|Measure Volume
menu Analyze|Measure Selection
move 312 262
down L 312 262
up L 312 262
dump
move 560 450
shot getting-started-12-measure gw
# Saved, and exported as STL.
file $tmp/plate.tlspr
key s ctrl
form
file $tmp/plate.stl
menu File|Export|Triangle Mesh (.stl, .3mf, .glb, .obj, .html, .js, .wrl)...
dump
